From: ai_re <ai_re@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:18:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] pci: add the Annapurna Labs Alpine V3 external PCIe
 root complex

Root complex driver for the Alpine V3 external PCIe ports, bound to the
node mainline Linux pcie-al uses ("amazon,al-alpine-v3-pcie": config,
controller and dbi regs). A HAL copy of its own (drivers/pci/al_pcie_v3,
not the Alpine V2 one of patch 0017): Annapurna's PCIe HAL, PBS utilities,
AVG SerDes lane driver, IOFIC and the Alpine V3 iomap, unmodified from
the MikroTik GPL Linux 5.6.3 source drop (drivers/soc/alpine/HAL; the
Annapurna files are triple-licensed and used under GPL-2.0, the Amazon
2017 files carry no licence of their own and are distributed as part of
that GPL kernel source), built with AL_DEV_ID = ALPINE_V3 (PCIe unit rev
4 only), plus U-Boot platform shims and a one-function SBus shim (the HAL
SBus driver with its embedded SBus master firmware is not built: PCIe
iCal talks to the lanes through their core-interrupt registers).

al_init_pcie_v3_rc.c is the RC path of the vendor al_init_pcie() with the
HAL's Alpine V3 default_init_pcie_params as al_pcie_init_adv() adjusts
them for an RC port; the vendor U-Boot 2018.05-alpine_db-v3.65.1 carries
the same template (gen3 lane EQ table 16 x {5, 0, 5, 0} at 0x011cd1f0,
gen3 params LF 6, FS 27, preset vector 0x10, FOM at 0x011cd230). New on
V3: per SerDes lane of the port (serdes_grp_objs_num = max lanes) the
firmware CRC/revision check, the eight-step PCIe iCal configuration
(interleaved across lanes) and the PCS interrupts, before the port config.

Probe: a link the firmware already trained is kept (chainloaded after
the vendor U-Boot); otherwise, with amazon,link-gen/-lanes and
amazon,serdes-lanes (main complex lane numbers), the port is initialised
as the vendor pci_init_board_external() does it (teardown on, link retry
off): one init at the DT gen/width; on failure half the lanes down to
x1, then Gen1 x1; a link that trains slower or narrower is kept and
reported. amazon,link-pre-delay-ms (the vendor rc-link-pre-delay, 100 ms)
once before the first port init, amazon,link-up-timeout-ms (its 100 ms
rc-link-up-timeout), amazon,crs-timeout-ms (crs-timeout, 30 s).

Config cycles, SError drain (U-Boot unmasks SErrors at EL2, an error
completion is an asynchronous SError on this SoC), CRS retry, iATU
region 0 and the bus numbering are those of the Alpine V2 driver.

OS handoff (DM_FLAG_OS_PREPARE remove): with amazon,endpoint-decode-off
the COMMAND register of the link partner's functions is cleared, the
state the vendor U-Boot leaves the CS8210 FPGAs in (Linux enables decode
itself; tools that touch a BAR before that assume it is off).

"alpcie status [port]" shows port, link, unit and partner registers;
"alpcie reinit <port>" removes the bus, tears the port down, runs the
full init and enumerates again. On a port that is not the last one probed
that leaves U-Boot's numbering of its bus higher (root port bus registers
no longer 1): reset before booting an OS after it.
PCIE_ALPINE_V3_FORCE_INIT (test builds only): every port gets the full
init at probe, i.e. the stage3 path in a RAM test after the vendor U-Boot,
with the cold-boot bus numbering.

Scope: alpine-v3.
